### Goal Model Decomposition

The mission involves managing food delivery and dish retrieval in a hospital setting, requiring a multi-robot system to handle tasks with or without human assistance. The goal model is structured to capture the hierarchical decomposition of goals into sub-goals and tasks, considering the system's requirements and uncertainties.

---

### Goal and Task Tables

#### Goals

| Name       | Text                                                                                     | Runtime                  | Goal Type   | Justification                                                                                     | Relation | Justification                                                                                     |
|------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------|-------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| G1         | Manage food delivery and dish retrieval efficiently.                                    | Sequential               | Achieve     | The mission requires sequential handling of delivery and retrieval.                                  | -        | -                                                                                               |
| G2         | Deliver food to the inpatient room.                                                     | -                        | Perform     | The goal is about executing the delivery action.                                                  | G1->G2   | G2 is part of the overall management and must be handled before or after retrieval.               |
| G3         | Retrieve dirty dishes from the inpatient room.                                           | -                        | Perform     | The goal is about executing the retrieval action.                                                  | G1->G3   | G3 is part of the overall management and must be handled after delivery.                          |
| G4         | Check if the inpatient can retrieve food from the robot's tray.                         | -                        | Query       | Necessary to determine if assistance is needed for delivery.                                       | G2->G4   | The information is required before proceeding with delivery.                                      |
| G5         | Check if someone is available to assist with dish retrieval.                             | -                        | Query       | Necessary to determine if assistance is needed for retrieval.                                      | G3->G5   | The information is required before proceeding with retrieval.                                      |
| G2.1       | Deliver food directly to the table using a special robot.                               | -                        | Perform     | Execution of direct delivery using a specialized robot.                                           | G2->G2.1 | This method is an alternative to tray delivery.                                                   |
| G2.2       | Deliver food via the robot's tray with human cooperation.                               | Sequential               | Perform     | Execution involves presenting the meal, indicating the correct one, and confirming retrieval.        | G2->G2.2 | Sequential steps are necessary to ensure correct meal retrieval.                                    |
| G3.1       | Retrieve dishes unassisted by a robot.                                                  | -                        | Perform     | Execution of unassisted dish retrieval.                                                           | G3->G3.1 | This is a possible method for dish retrieval.                                                     |
| G3.2       | Retrieve dishes with the cooperation of another robot.                                  | -                        | Perform     | Execution involves two robots working together.                                                   | G3->G3.2 | This method is an alternative for dish retrieval when one robot isn't sufficient.                  |
| G3.3       | Retrieve dishes with human cooperation.                                                  | -                        | Perform     | Execution involves a robot and a human working together.                                           | G3->G3.3 | This method is an alternative for dish retrieval when no robots are available.                     |

